PART 2 -- the convolution bound, at the frequencies where W3 is most biased
 phi(beta) magnitudes, averaged over the 40 contexts as sqrt(T/(ngrp)) / sqrt(n_per_ctx):
  beta | |phi_W3|  |phi_s0(W4)|  product   |phi_c3| observed   noise floor
  1         0.15515    0.02504     0.003885   0.02617            0.02413  <-- product predicts observed
  2         0.07916    0.02620     0.002074   0.02385            0.02413  
  3         0.06026    0.02479     0.001494   0.02737            0.02413  
  4         0.04622    0.03029     0.001400   0.02673            0.02413  
  5         0.03935    0.02278     0.000896   0.02273            0.02413  
  8         0.03320    0.02186     0.000726   0.02103            0.02413  
  16        0.02893    0.02321     0.000671   0.02276            0.02413  
  65536     0.02667    0.02977     0.000794   0.02614            0.02413  
  16777216  0.02327    0.02225     0.000518   0.02474            0.02413  

  => entropy deficit contributed by a frequency: dH ~ |phi|^2/ln2 bits (per +-beta pair).
     W3 alone at beta=1 : |phi|=0.1551  -> 0.0347 bits of deficit in W3
     s0(W4) at beta=1   : |phi|=0.0250  (noise floor 0.0241) -> consistent with 0
     c3 at beta=1       : |phi|=0.0262  (noise floor 0.0241) -> 9.88e-04 bits
     HARD CAP: even a table policy driving |phi_W3(1)| -> 1.0 gives |phi_c3(1)| <= 0.0250
              i.e. at most 9.05e-04 bits of speedup from that frequency.

